GARUDA changes to the OpenCores I2C controllers (D-22, zero-waiver F4, recorded 2026-11-19).
Richard Herveille's notice is kept in both files.
- F4 renames (d995a4a): clock and reset ports to pclk/preset_n; i2c_master_bit_ctrl ->
  i2c_bit_ctrl and i2c_master_byte_ctrl -> i2c_byte_ctrl (HAL module-name length).
- F4 style (a7c8db1): tools/rtl_style.py; proven equivalent by JasperGold SEC.
- 2026-11-18: the `#1` delays on nonblocking assignments in the byte controller removed
  (yosys-slang rejects them for synthesis; simulation-only, no logic change; TOOL-A23).

